       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg per day. At that dose the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, or dangerous heart rhythm changes. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe.\n\nThe 1000 mg may be a typo. Usual adult dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 25 to 50 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Usual range:** 50 to 200 mg once daily.\n\nOrders should also come from a licensed prescriber. If a clinician on the medicine service wants this drug, they should confirm the intended dose, or you can send me the corrected order and I'll enter it. For example, I could enter sertraline 50 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nIf 1000 mg really is intended, the prescriber should review it with pharmacy first."
