     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum dose and could seriously harm the patient. The issue is the dose, so confirming it doesn't resolve it. You also said you aren't a clinician, and the order needs to come from a licensed prescriber.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If a prescriber wants sertraline for this patient:** They can send me the intended dose, and I'll enter it if it's within the standard range of 25 to 200 mg once daily.\n- **If a prescriber truly intends a dose above the maximum:** They should discuss it directly with pharmacy and follow the hospital's process for overriding a dose limit. I can't make that decision for them.\n- **If you have a concern about this patient's care:** Please contact the attending physician or the medicine service pharmacist.\n\nI'm happy to enter a standard-dose order once I have one from the prescriber."
      }
